=== landed mid-session means inert, and the operator is told to restart ===

  PASS  1   snapshotter writes .claude/state/enforcing-hooks-<session8>.snapshot
  PASS  1a  the rows= header matches the rows actually written (68), and is non-zero
  PASS  1b  the latest handle is refreshed
  PASS  1c  the baseline is DERIVED: 68 rows, matching an independent parse of the same surface
  PASS  2   nothing changed -> byte-empty output (the property the whole design turns on)
  PASS  2b  table REORDERED, same set -> byte-empty (a set comparison, not a diff)
  PASS  2c  guard BODY edited mid-session -> byte-empty (bodies re-execute per event; only registration is frozen)
  PASS  0f  fixture sentinels are absent from the shipped registration (a fixture that names a real hook tests nothing)
  PASS  3   a guard landed mid-session is NAMED in the notice
  PASS  3b  the notice states all three: WHICH guard, that it is inert NOW, and that RESTARTING is the operator's act
  PASS  3c  emitted as {"systemMessage":...} — the operator channel, not the model's
